  "details": "EAC prevents launching the game with valid UnityPlayer.dll signed and issued by Unity from win64_development_il2cpp variation.\nThis version of UnityPlayer.dll is absolute legit and compatible and can be used to switch game build development variation adding new features forc reators such as profiling and frame debugging. A very useful tool allows to see bottlenecks on real game with real players and real conditions in VR, instead of poorly imitated environment in Unity Editor. This variation is made by Unity and does not allow to load mods, expose specific internal data, rip something or do something eles malicious. It's purpose to give creator access to monitoring the game resources, it's usage, timings, loads, ratios and bottlenecks. I used this tool before to find problems in my and friends worlds, and to figure out shader issues on avatars using in specific worlds conditions using frame debbuger/captures. It was even useful to monitor Udon before EventDispatcher became in charge. I believe UnityPlayer.dll from win64_development_il2cpp variation should be allowed by EAC.",
